meta {
  name: Sync Email
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/email-sync
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "from_date": "2026-07-01"
  }
}

docs {
  The `202 Accepted` response identifies the sync job:

  ```json
  {"job_id":"sync-job","status_url":"/jobs/sync-job"}
  ```

  Open **Jobs / Check Job** with that `job_id`. A successful sync result links to the
  template-assignment job that was submitted after synchronization:

  ```json
  {
    "pulled": 7,
    "inserted": 3,
    "already_stored": 4,
    "template_assignment_job_id": "assignment-job"
  }
  ```

  Check `assignment-job` through the same job endpoint. Its result links every newly
  created template to its independent parser-generation job:

  ```json
  {
    "processed": 3,
    "skipped": 0,
    "templates_created": 1,
    "created_template_ids": [12],
    "parser_generation_jobs": [
      {"template_id": 12, "job_id": "parser-job"}
    ]
  }
  ```

  Check each parser `job_id` separately. Parser failures do not change the completed sync
  or template-assignment results, and transaction extraction is not started automatically.
}
